<title>USA: Network sector bounds back on positive USRX report.</title>
<headline>Network sector bounds back on positive USRX report.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Networking stocks regained their footing Tuesday as the sector posted strong gains following U.S. Robotics Inc's upbeat earnings report and ahead of sector flagship Cisco Systems Inc's own report.</p>
<p>NatWest analyst Steve Koffler said U.S. Robotics' report restored faith among jittery investors who feared the sector's momentum might be slowing. &quot;I think people are looking at (the USRX report) as a positive for the whole sector,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>In addition, investors bid up Ascend Communications Inc on news it would introduce a device to allow Internet providers to accept calls from higher speed 56-kilobit modems.</p>
</text>
